      "directNodeIds": [
        "math:real-exponent-laws",
        "cnm_196"
      ],
      "explanation": "Increasing the exponent of \\(4\\) by \\(1\\) multiplies its value by \\(4\\). Thus, for every real \\(x\\),\n\\[\nf(x+1)=4^{x+1}=4\\cdot4^x=4f(x).\n\\]\nSubtracting \\(f(x)\\) gives\n\\[\nf(x+1)-f(x)=4f(x)-f(x)=\\boxed{3f(x)}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
      "id": "shift-exponent-by-one",
      "sourceRef": "amc/1967_AMC_12_Q06#shift-exponent-by-one",
      "title": "Use the exponent-sum law"
    }
